# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Other hosts ignore this file.
#
# There is no SPA catch-all here on purpose: every public page is prerendered to
# its own index.html by scripts/prerender.mjs, so the host serves real files and
# unknown paths fall through to 404.html, which is also prerendered.
#
# The result portal needs the board's API reachable at a same-origin path. This
# rule gets the three GET endpoints through, but NOT the lookup: the board
# answers POST /result with 403 unless the request's Origin is its own, and a
# redirect rule cannot set an outgoing request header. Put a function or worker
# in front of the board on these hosts — see "The Origin header" in the README.
/api/public/*  https://result.bteb.gov.bd/api/public/:splat  200
